WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Treasure Island

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:18.630
<i>Mother and I somehow succeeded in escaping the pirates.</i>

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:35.010
<i>And we've opened the rumored chest of Billy Bones.</i>

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.770
<i>But who knew there'd be a map of Treasure Island inside!</i>

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.880
Treasure
Island

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.680
Takarajima

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.490
saa ikou

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.490
Come, let's go

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:57.580
yume ni mita shima heto

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:57.580
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:01.420
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:01.420
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.300
umi hedeyou

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.300
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.220
ikute ni wa

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.220
Many of us

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.220
minna mada shiranai

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.220
Still don't know of

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.970
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.970
The days and nights full of mystery

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.470
matte iru darou

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.470
That await us there

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.980
itsumo shinji you

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.980
We must always have trust

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:23.230
magokoro wo

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:23.230
And be sincere

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:29.490
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:29.490
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:32.620
tade hitotsu no

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:32.620
I only...

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:36.040
akogare dake wa

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:36.040
...have one desire

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:38.330
doko no dare ni mo

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:38.330
And no one...

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:45.040
kese wa shinai sa

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:45.040
...will ever take it away

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.590
tade hitotsu no

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.590
I only...

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.890
akogare dake wa

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.890
...have one desire

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.220
doko no dare ni mo

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.220
And no one...

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:04.150
kese wa shinai sa

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:04.150
...will ever take it away

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:15.070
episode

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:15.070
See you later,
            mom!

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.080
<i>A reef,</i>

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.630
<i>Skeleton Island,</i>

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:29.330
<i>a fort,</i>

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:30.630
<i>a tomb...</i>

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.230
<i>"Bulk of Treasure" ?</i>

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:37.510
<i>"August 1750, Captain Flint."</i>

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:41.330
There's no doubt.
It's definitely Flint's treasure.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.390
Flint, that terrible pirate...

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:49.850
<i>He scoured for years on the world's seven seas.</i>

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:54.940
<i>During his travels he amassed a fortune beyond imagining.</i>

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:58.390
<i>Flint was truly one of the
greatest pirates of all time.</i>

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:03.380
Jim really got his hands on an invaluable document...

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.780
Mr. Trelawney.
Mr. Trelawney!

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:13.950
Why won't you let me come with you?

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.110
Because I'm too young?

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:19.070
You know, I can work as much as an adult.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.970
I can do the dishes, make the food,
wash the deck...

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.470
Just about anything, you see.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.010
I won't be a burden to you.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:29.310
So take me along to Treasure Island.
Please, Mr. Trelawney.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:33.190
Captain Billy gave the map to <i>me.</i>

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.890
And yet, you want me to stand aside—

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.320
Mr. Trelawney!

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:48.700
Mr. Trelawney!

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:51.150
Calm down, I understand.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.510
Tell me, Jim—

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:54.470
So you'll take me with you?

00:03:54.470 --> 00:03:58.130
You must be hungry, right?
Breakfast is ready.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:01.090
Dang!

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:17.860
What's wrong Jim, you're not eating?

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.070
I don't feel like it.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:21.900
A child must eat if he wants to grow—

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.950
I'm not a child anymore!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:27.600
I know, I know.
Don't get riled up.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:38.090
Treasure Island...

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.150
I won't give up.

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:51.230
"Point toward N.-N.-E.
a quarter N.,"

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:53.510
"foothills of the Spyglass..."

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:58.070
"Big tree...
Skeleton Island, E.-S.-E. a quarter E."

00:04:58.070 --> 00:04:59.820
What gibberish...

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:03.780
In short, the location of the treasure isn't clearly indicated.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.580
I see, that makes sense.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:11.630
That must mean Flint's treasure is absolutely fabulous beyond anything one can imagine.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:14.510
One that would suit only
the most fearless of men.

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:18.030
A great adventure for men of worth.
Like in the books.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:20.300
My heart is beating wildly!

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.640
My blood is <i>literally</i> boiling, I'd say!

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.350
Raise the anchor!
Hoist the mainsail!

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:31.150
Helm to starboard!
Head for Treasure Island!

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:36.940
By the way, Trelawney.
Where's Jim in all this?

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:39.470
Livesey, I'm counting on you.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:42.400
You must convince him to not come along.

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:48.260
Jim, how old are you now?

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:49.160
13 years old.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.250
I see, 13 years old, huh?

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.910
How peculiar.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:55.120
What is?

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.070
When I was your age,

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:01.100
I also dreamt of going out to sea.

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:01.990
Really?

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:03.510
You too, Dr. Livesey?

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:07.710
And finally, at my current age,
my wish came true.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:09.970
It isn't the age to attempt an adventure.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:14.760
I'm not against the idea
of you accompanying us.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:16.780
D-Do you meant that?

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:19.110
However...

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:22.290
I have one condition.

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:25.990
You can't see it from here,
but behind those cliffs you'll find...

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:27.700
...the Benbow Inn.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:31.950
There your mother works alone with all her might.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.540
Jim, have you thought of your mother?

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.370
You intend to leave her all alone?

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:03.590
The treasure map is safe with Livesey.

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:08.630
I'm leaving for Bristol to buy a ship and hire a crew.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.850
I can't wait to take to sea.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:20.030
By the way, Jim.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.080
I just got an excellent idea.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.590
An excellent idea?

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:25.550
You heard right.

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.550
From time to time, I will send you a letter.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:33.050
How about that? I will describe our journey in great detail.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:38.590
By reading these letters, you can live the adventure as if you were there.

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:41.850
Now that I think about it,
it really is a good idea, yes.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.250
We've arrived.

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:49.670
Bye, Jim.
Take care.

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:54.280
<i>Mr. Trelawney doesn't understand.</i>

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:56.620
<i>He can send me all the letters he want,</i>

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:00.650
<i>but it's meaningless if I can't live the adventure for real.</i>

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:14.950
<i>The next day I helped my mother repair the inn that the pirates wrecked with all my might.</i>

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:19.560
<i>But I haven't given up on Treasure Island.</i>

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:27.170
It's finished!

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:29.190
Yup, perfect.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:35.330
I'll take care of downstairs.

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:38.390
Jim, take care of room three meanwhile.

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:40.240
Aye-aye, sir!

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:43.330
Everything is upside down,
so I'm counting on you.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:44.820
Got it!

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:49.890
It's me, Captain!

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:51.800
What am I saying?

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:56.660
What a disaster...

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:59.600
Okay, I'll throw out the stuff
that we can't use.

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:04.020
Well, this is useless.

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:06.320
This too.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:07.610
So is this.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:09.950
And this and this and this...

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:12.600
Really, pretty much everything will be thrown out.

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:25.290
Captain Billy...

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:40.180
<i>In the end, the only place for a true sailor to die, is out on sea.</i>

00:09:45.590 --> 00:09:46.440
That was fast—

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:51.890
Jim...

00:09:52.510 --> 00:09:55.610
I'm going to bury this at
the cliff by the sea, okay?

00:09:57.970 --> 00:10:01.580
I see.
Yes, I think that's a good idea.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:06.120
Hey, wait for me, Benbow!

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:11.290
It's on!
I won't lose.

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:18.800
Little devil!

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:30.730
Captain Billy,

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:33.990
I'm sure that this place by
the sea suits you perfectly.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:51.960
Captain Billy...

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:55.920
It's decided, I will go to sea.

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:36.880
Jim!

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:40.380
What are you doing?

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:41.840
Treasure hunting!

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:52.690
<i>The kid doesn't seem to be there...</i>

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:55.410
Who is it?
Is there anyone there?

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:58.940
Madam, are you there?
Madam!

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:02.400
I have a letter for you!
It comes from Bristol!

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:05.990
Do you have to leave?

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:10.410
Yeah! I'm going after the treasure!
The treasure of the pirate, Flint.

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:11.970
You've already decided?

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:14.830
You bet! I mustn't let
this chance pass me by.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.090
I'm going for sure!

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:21.690
Then I'll help your mother at the Benbow Inn while you're away.

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:24.270
It will be hard for her, all alone...

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:28.600
<i>Are you going to leave your mom all alone?</i>

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:39.640
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...!

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:41.130
If I were a boy,

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:43.250
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum!

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:44.660
I'd go with him to search for Treasure Island.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:47.620
Drink and the devil had done for the rest...

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:54.160
Jim, dinner's ready!

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:56.650
Come down quickly or else your soup will get cold.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:59.170
Sure, I'll be there shortly!

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:01.190
You understand it all, right Dad?

00:13:01.190 --> 00:13:04.430
I just have to convince Mom.
Don't you agree, Dad?

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:12.180
Delicious!
That was really good.

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:15.980
Mom, I want to talk to you about something.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:16.560
I'm listening.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:18.930
You see, for example...

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:22.250
I'm saying "if ever", 'kay?

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:25.490
If I... ever, you know,
wanted to go out to sea...

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:29.450
By, let's say, myself...
Again, it's just an example...

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:33.240
Basically, Mom, if I were to say that...

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.040
...how would you reply?

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:37.290
Oh right, I completely forgot.

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:39.750
A letter came from Mr. Trelawney.

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:41.870
A letter?

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:44.700
As for what you were you trying to tell me...

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:46.680
Y-Yes?

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:49.640
I'm sorry, but I didn't quite catch any of it.

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:53.670
\{Uh well... \}I'll tell you... tomorrow in more detail, okay?

00:13:57.250 --> 00:14:02.110
<i>If I leave with them, Mom will be all alone...</i>

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:05.160
<i>...and that is something that poses a problem.</i>

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:07.530
<i>But at the same time,</i>

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:09.910
<i>I've decided to go.</i>

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:12.200
<i>Dad, what should I do at a time like this?</i>

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:15.040
Really, what should I do, Dad?

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:18.740
Tell me what I should do, Benbow.

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:31.590
<i>That night, I read the letter from Mr. Trelawney.</i>

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:34.310
<i>"Jim, I have very good news."</i>

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:37.410
<i>"I bought an absolutely magnificent ship."</i>

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:41.560
<i>"It is a schooner with three masts:
The Hispaniola."</i>

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:44.900
<i>"I was able to find this ship,</i>

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:47.870
<i>thanks to a one-legged man from the Spyglass."</i>

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:49.320
A one-legged man?

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:52.810
<i>"He's an incredible man."</i>

00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:57.790
<i>"He seems to be acquainted to all the sailors in Bristol."</i>

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:00.030
<i>"Also, he has a lot of experience with the sea."</i>

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:05.710
<i>"So when he told me that he was looking for a good place as a master cook,</i>

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:09.420
<i>without thinking twice,
I hired him on the spot."</i>

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:13.430
<i>"He even introduced us to a group of old sea dogs."</i>

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:15.630
<i>"All of them strong fellows."</i>

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:18.270
<i>"We are almost ready to sail."</i>

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.850
<i>"Oh, the sea!
Oh, Treasure Island!"</i>

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:26.190
<i>"My heart has taken to sea and
sails towards adventure already!"</i>

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:30.070
<i>"Jim, I will write you another letter when I have more news."</i>

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:34.240
Treasure Island...
Treasure Island, Treasure Island...

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:38.130
<i>There's no time to lose!</i>

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:40.040
<i>According to this letter,</i>

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:42.130
<i>they won't wait to sail.</i>

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:46.960
<i>I must at all costs talk to my mother and get her permission.</i>

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:01.690
'Kay, I'm going to practice so that I don't mumble the whole time.

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:05.030
"Mom, I have something to tell you."

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:08.240
"What is it, Jim?
You seem serious..."

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:11.250
"Mom, I want to go!"

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:12.370
"Go where?"

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:14.570
"To the sea!
To Treasure Island!"

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:19.040
"I will go to venture with
Mr. Trelawney and Dr. Livesey."

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:24.010
"And you're going to leave
your poor mother all alone?"

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:26.010
"I've thought about it a lot,

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:28.960
but I really want to go to sea!"

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:31.590
<i>I want to go on an adventure, Mom!</i>

00:16:39.050 --> 00:16:41.390
<i>My dear, Jim is now 13 years old.</i>

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:43.780
<i>Perhaps it's time that he lives his life.</i>

00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:50.110
<i>And besides, you too went to sea
for the first time at the age of 13.</i>

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:57.690
B-Black Dog...

00:16:57.690 --> 00:17:00.540
Yo, kid.
I have a question to ask you.

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:04.010
Tell me who has Billy Bone's map.

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:06.500
Is it Livesey?
Or maybe Trelawney?

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:09.250
I know nothing of it!

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:12.920
You refuse to talk?!

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:18.310
Stay there!

00:17:29.010 --> 00:17:31.610
Now, tell me who has the map!

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:32.990
I don't know!

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:36.800
Hey, brat!
Talk or I cut you in two.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.820
Stop! Let him go!

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:42.740
M-Mom!

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:46.870
Don't meddle in this or you'll suffer, woman!

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:49.530
It's you who'll be in trouble!

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:52.530
There are around ten young men at the inn.

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:55.050
If I call, they will come out!

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:59.090
Now, let go of my son and be quick about it!

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:04.010
Everyone help! A pirate!

00:18:03.860 --> 00:18:05.980
A pirate!

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:05.980
Curses!

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:10.250
Come quick everyone, there's a pirate!

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:09.690
Damn you!

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:12.430
You'll pay for this!

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:16.290
And don't come back!

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:18.200
You alright, Jim?

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:20.030
Who do you think I am?!

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:23.530
No mere pirate will give me a hard time!

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:27.260
Is that so?
Yet you seemed to be in quite a pickle.

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:30.260
I was toying with him.
I had things under control.

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:32.050
By the way, who are those young men?

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:35.700
That was all a bluff!

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:38.220
Not bad, huh?
I, too, can take care of myself.

00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:46.060
What a feast!

00:18:46.490 --> 00:18:49.100
Say, what is the occasion?

00:18:51.490 --> 00:18:54.590
Jim, didn't you have something important to tell me?

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:55.690
Something important?

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:57.570
Yes, something important.

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.660
Yesterday you tried to tell me something.

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:05.410
Go ahead, I'm listening.
Tell me everything.

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:10.070
Then I'll tell you everything.

00:19:10.070 --> 00:19:14.250
Mom, I want to go to sea to search for Treasure Island!

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:16.580
Can I go, Mom?
Can I? Can I?

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:23.970
Yes, you have my permission, Jim.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:25.680
R-R—

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:27.330
Yes, really.

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:30.250
I've written a letter to
Mr. Trelawney and Dr. Livesey...

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:32.650
...asking them to take you with them.

00:19:36.930 --> 00:19:39.030
Treasure Island here we come!

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.410
On to Treasure Island!

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:43.280
I prepared this meal to
celebrate your departure.

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:47.210
I promise...
I'll bring you back the treasure.

00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:50.090
Then you can open a second Benbow Inn in London.

00:19:50.090 --> 00:19:53.330
A second Admiral Benbow Inn,
deluxe edition!

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:55.710
That's right,
we have every right to dream.

00:19:56.830 --> 00:20:00.070
<i>Three days later, I received a letter from Bristol.</i>

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:03.400
<i>And of course, they agreed to take me with them.</i>

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:05.950
<i>Then again, three days after that,</i>

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:10.210
<i>Mr. Trelawney sent Old Redruth to fetch me.</i>

00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:12.850
Wait a second, Jim.

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:15.270
I haven't finished packing everything.

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:16.280
You're adding more?

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:20.070
What are you talking about?
One can never have too many clothes.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:24.290
What's down that way—

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:27.830
Here, this was your father's spyglass.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:28.570
Mom...

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:32.090
It isn't brand new, but it'll be of use to you.

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:33.250
Thank you.

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:46.690
Hey!
Jim Hawkins, I'm here!

00:20:46.690 --> 00:20:47.680
Are you ready?

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:51.180
Mom, he's here!
Here he is! Here he is!

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:52.770
Go on, Jim.

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:56.780
Dad! Jim Hawkins reporting, ready to set sail!

00:20:56.780 --> 00:20:58.850
I leave Mom in your care.

00:20:59.450 --> 00:21:00.980
You rascal...

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:03.250
Sorry for the wait!

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:16.290
Mom...

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:20.440
Today's a good day!

00:21:20.440 --> 00:21:22.130
It's a perfect day to travel.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:22.920
That's true.

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:25.180
Okay, I'm going, Mom.

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:26.930
Have a safe trip, Jim.

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:34.270
Bye!

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:38.230
Jim, pay attention to the water you drink.
Take good care of your body!

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:42.410
Don't you worry!
I'm a man now!

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:43.970
<i>That's true...</i>

00:21:43.970 --> 00:21:46.700
<i>You're already a young man, aren't you?</i>

00:22:00.050 --> 00:22:01.210
Jim!

00:22:02.450 --> 00:22:05.170
Lilly!
I'm counting on you!

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:08.130
Jim, take care!

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:11.810
The village will be very lonely without him.

00:22:18.350 --> 00:22:20.690
<i>And now, head for Treasure Island!</i>

00:22:27.620 --> 00:22:31.620
To      be        continued

00:22:32.650 --> 00:22:37.690
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:32.650 --> 00:22:37.690
Hey sea breeze

00:22:37.690 --> 00:22:43.500
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:37.690 --> 00:22:43.500
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:44.720 --> 00:22:49.710
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:44.720 --> 00:22:49.710
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:49.710 --> 00:22:55.150
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:49.710 --> 00:22:55.150
A word to my dear mother

00:22:55.150 --> 00:23:00.560
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:55.150 --> 00:23:00.560
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:06.020
kaban ippai no

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:06.020
And that my bag filled

00:23:06.020 --> 00:23:11.650
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:06.020 --> 00:23:11.650
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:11.650 --> 00:23:17.510
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:11.650 --> 00:23:17.510
Will be brought back

00:23:18.600 --> 00:23:24.100
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:18.600 --> 00:23:24.100
The sunset on my back

00:23:24.100 --> 00:23:29.990
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:24.100 --> 00:23:29.990
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:29.990 --> 00:23:39.710
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:29.990 --> 00:23:39.710
I blow out a whistle

00:23:44.450 --> 00:23:47.090
Before our adventure's grand departure,

00:23:47.090 --> 00:23:50.470
I must make acquaintance with John Silver, a one-legged man.

00:23:50.470 --> 00:23:53.530
This one-legged man will be
the master cook on our ship...

00:23:53.530 --> 00:23:54.410
Remember?

00:23:54.410 --> 00:23:58.770
"This man isn't the one-legged man that Captain Billy was afraid of."

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:01.900
Although this is what Mr. Trelawney and Dr. Livesey said,

00:24:01.900 --> 00:24:04.290
I prefer to check for myself.

00:24:04.890 --> 00:24:08.490
Next time on Treasure Island:
"John Silver; Friend or Foe?"

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:12.720
Next time

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:12.720
Coming soon!

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:12.720
John Silver;
Friend Or Foe?

00:24:08.490 --> 00:24:09.670
That sounds promising!
